The NA62 experiment has carried out the first dedicated investigation of the $K^+ightarrow\pi^+
u ar{
u}$ channel using data collected in 2016 with a beam intensity of about 2x10^11 protons. A search for the rare decay of negatively charged kaons within the transverse momentum range of 10 to 60 GeV/c, and pseudorapidity range of 0.5 to 1.5, was undertaken. Results from this research indicate that out of 7.26 x 10^12 analysed decays, one occurrence of $K^+ightarrow\pi^+
u ar{
u}$ is observed at a frequency of (0.82$\pm$0.65$\pm$0.13) x 10^-5, corresponding to a standard model prediction at 90% confidence level.
